  minoxidil. Seven of the twelve subjects assayed in the minoxidil group had detectable minoxidil serum levels,         
  ranging from 0.4 to 7.5 ng/ml.'}, {'study_index': 5, 'title': 'Topical minoxidil (3%) in extensive alopecia areata,   
  including long-term efficacy', 'abstract': 'This study was conducted to further evaluate the safety and efficacy of   
  3% topical minoxidil in the treatment of extensive alopecia areata. Patients were assigned to one of two treatment    
  regimens in a double-blind manner. One group applied 3% minoxidil to the scalp twice daily for 64 weeks; the other    
